1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:03,962
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,885 --> 00:00:12,178
[Jepoy] <i>Will you just stand there</i>

3
00:00:12,262 --> 00:00:14,139
<i>while Ivy and Arnaldo get married?!</i>

4
00:00:14,222 --> 00:00:16,558
[Ivy] <i>Jepoy, shouldn't you be</i>
<i>the one who understands the most</i>

5
00:00:16,641 --> 00:00:18,852
<i>why I need to marry Arnaldo?!</i>

6
00:00:18,935 --> 00:00:20,270
[Jepoy] <i>I'll support her plan.</i>

7
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:23,857
<i>But I'll find another way</i>
<i>to bring down the Ardientes.</i>

8
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:27,444
<i>I would like you to take care</i>
<i>of one of our enemies.</i>

9
00:00:27,527 --> 00:00:28,820
<i>Kill Jaguar.</i>

10
00:00:28,903 --> 00:00:31,031
<i>For the sake of our family.</i>

11
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:33,241
[Raul] <i>So, you're really</i>
<i>going to kill Jaguar?</i>

12
00:00:33,324 --> 00:00:34,284
<i>Can you do it?</i>

13
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:35,410
<i>Ping!</i>

14
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:37,829
[Emilia] <i>Who are you?!</i>

15
00:00:37,912 --> 00:00:39,289
[grunts]

16
00:00:39,372 --> 00:00:40,832
[Raul] <i>Rufo, I need your help.</i>

17
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:42,792
[Emilia] <i>Where were you?</i>

18
00:00:42,876 --> 00:00:44,794
[Raul] <i>I'm right here, taking a bath.</i>

19
00:00:47,630 --> 00:00:49,299
[Anthony] <i>Thank you for coming here today</i>

20
00:00:49,382 --> 00:00:51,676
<i>for the Poblacion Ardiente public debate.</i>

21
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:54,137
<i>You haven't been in any</i>
<i>government position before.</i>

22
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:55,472
<i>Wouldn't it be better</i>

23
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:57,432
<i>if our lives all improved together?</i>

24
00:00:57,515 --> 00:00:59,350
[Anthony] <i>You are running out</i>
<i>of time, Mayor.</i>

25
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:01,811
<i>Mayor!</i>

26
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:05,106
[Ivy] <i>I think it's time the public learns</i>

27
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:08,401
<i>that my future husband</i>
<i>is going through something.</i>

28
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:10,570
<i>What do you mean? Is the mayor sick?</i>

29
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:13,323
[Ivy] <i>I guess that's all</i>
<i>I can say for now.</i>

30
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:14,491
[Julio] <i>Tell me the truth.</i>

31
00:01:14,574 --> 00:01:18,119
<i>What happened, that you had</i>
<i>to walk out during the debate?</i>

32
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:20,497
<i>Please tell me.</i>

33
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:21,998
[Arnaldo] <i>They're in front of me.</i>

34
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:23,458
<i>Carlotta and Nimfa…</i>

35
00:01:23,541 --> 00:01:25,251
<i>They're haunting me!</i>

36
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:26,878
<i>They're alive!</i>

37
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:29,297
<i>I don't know what's happening!</i>
<i>I don't know!</i>

38
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:31,758
<i>I… I don't know what to do!</i>

39
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:37,096
[Arnaldo crying]

40
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:39,224
It's okay. It's all right.

41
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:40,809
-Grandpa.
-Go and rest.

42
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:42,519
-Go and rest.
-But… [sniffles]

43
00:01:42,602 --> 00:01:43,978
Go and rest. Go to your bed.

44
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:45,021
-[Arnaldo sobs]
-Sleep.

45
00:01:45,104 --> 00:01:47,398
We'll talk again tomorrow, all right?

46
00:01:47,482 --> 00:01:50,401
Don't worry. I'll be here.
I'll be here for you.

47
00:01:50,485 --> 00:01:53,321
I will always be here for you, okay?

48
00:01:53,988 --> 00:01:55,281
Stop crying. Come on, my son.

49
00:01:55,365 --> 00:01:56,407
Come on.

50
00:01:56,908 --> 00:01:58,284
Go ahead. Go ahead.

51
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:00,286
Tomorrow is another day.

52
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:01,621
Forget it. Forget it.

53
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:02,747
Forget it.

54
00:02:03,289 --> 00:02:04,415
Forget it. They're not real.

55
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:05,625
Forget it.

56
00:02:05,708 --> 00:02:07,001
[sighs]

57
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:08,461
Forget it.

58
00:02:09,587 --> 00:02:10,588
Go ahead.

59
00:02:11,464 --> 00:02:12,715
Go. We'll talk again.

60
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:13,925
Everything will be different.

61
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:15,927
Everything will be fine tomorrow.

62
00:02:16,719 --> 00:02:17,804
It's okay.

63
00:02:18,596 --> 00:02:20,723
-It's okay, my son. It's okay.
-[Arnaldo sniffles]

64
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:22,475
Go and rest.

65
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:33,945
[breath quivering]

66
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:40,535
[sobbing]

67
00:02:53,965 --> 00:03:00,722
[tense music playing]

68
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:14,027
[tense music playing]

69
00:03:17,447 --> 00:03:18,656
Who are you?

70
00:03:21,993 --> 00:03:23,036
Speak up.

71
00:03:24,162 --> 00:03:25,413
I just got lost.

72
00:03:27,957 --> 00:03:32,629
[tense music playing]

73
00:03:32,712 --> 00:03:33,880
Got lost?

74
00:03:36,216 --> 00:03:37,842
All right, leave.

75
00:03:38,426 --> 00:03:39,552
Turn around.

76
00:03:43,848 --> 00:03:47,936
[tense music playing]

77
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:49,604
Scram.

78
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:56,778
Leave!

79
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:04,369
Just so you know,

80
00:04:04,452 --> 00:04:06,871
the first two private
investigators I hired

81
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:10,583
now both have permanent residency in hell.

82
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:13,670
I'm sure you don't want
to join them, do you?

83
00:04:14,587 --> 00:04:16,673
Now, what's the dirt on Lily Cruz?

84
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:18,758
She's spotless, Ma'am Emilia.

85
00:04:19,592 --> 00:04:20,927
What do you mean?

86
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:22,387
She really is Lily Cruz.

87
00:04:23,054 --> 00:04:25,348
<i>She's a high school teacher</i>
<i>in some province.</i>

88
00:04:25,431 --> 00:04:27,392
<i>She's an active member</i>
<i>of her town's organization.</i>

89
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:29,018
She's an exemplary citizen.

90
00:04:31,479 --> 00:04:32,563
And other than that,

91
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:35,358
what else did you find
about that Lily Cruz?

92
00:04:35,441 --> 00:04:37,610
What distracted my son during the debate?

93
00:04:37,694 --> 00:04:41,281
[tense music playing]

94
00:04:42,073 --> 00:04:42,949
She's an orphan.

95
00:04:43,408 --> 00:04:46,536
<i>Her aunt, who worked overseas,</i>
<i>raised her for 10 years.</i>

96
00:04:47,245 --> 00:04:48,371
When the woman died,

97
00:04:48,871 --> 00:04:50,832
Lily Cruz inherited everything she owned.

98
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:54,335
Oh, so she has no family.

99
00:04:54,419 --> 00:04:55,753
Now, it makes sense.

100
00:04:55,837 --> 00:04:59,215
That's why she can afford
to dress herself properly.

101
00:04:59,799 --> 00:05:00,800
So…

102
00:05:01,801 --> 00:05:03,970
When did this aunt die?

103
00:05:04,929 --> 00:05:07,932
[tense music playing]

104
00:05:08,016 --> 00:05:11,853
[phone ringing]

105
00:05:13,646 --> 00:05:14,605
Jepoy.

106
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:15,481
Ivy.

107
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:17,608
Jepoy, I need your help.

108
00:05:17,692 --> 00:05:18,901
What's wrong?

109
00:05:19,485 --> 00:05:20,445
<i>It's Emilia.</i>

110
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:22,864
She's doing a background check on Anna

111
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:24,699
because she thinks Anna did something

112
00:05:24,782 --> 00:05:26,701
to cause Arnaldo
to walk out of the debate.

113
00:05:27,243 --> 00:05:28,578
Don't worry about it.

114
00:05:28,661 --> 00:05:29,746
Before we even came back,

115
00:05:29,829 --> 00:05:31,748
I took care of Anna's background.

116
00:05:31,831 --> 00:05:34,625
They won't find anything
about her real identity.

117
00:05:34,917 --> 00:05:36,961
Thank you, Jepoy.

118
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:39,047
I know I can always count on you,

119
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:42,842
even if you don't agree
with my plan right now.

120
00:05:45,803 --> 00:05:46,804
<i>Ivy…</i>

121
00:05:48,473 --> 00:05:51,059
It doesn't matter what I think or feel.

122
00:05:51,142 --> 00:05:53,644
<i>You know I'll always support you.</i>

123
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:56,105
But you'll have to forgive me.

124
00:05:56,773 --> 00:05:58,107
I'll keep finding another way.

125
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:00,359
Thanks.

126
00:06:03,446 --> 00:06:08,576
[tense music playing]

127
00:06:11,913 --> 00:06:13,122
Emilia?

128
00:06:15,041 --> 00:06:16,084
Ivy.

129
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:22,048
Thanks for the statement
you released to the press

130
00:06:22,131 --> 00:06:23,758
about Arnaldo, by the way.

131
00:06:24,717 --> 00:06:28,012
At least now, people know
he's not feeling well.

132
00:06:28,096 --> 00:06:30,807
But, on the other hand, with what you did,

133
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:33,351
people might think that he's weak.

134
00:06:33,434 --> 00:06:35,436
No, that's not necessarily the case.

135
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,147
It could've helped him gain
the support of the voters.

136
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:42,610
Did I just hear you talking
to a private investigator?

137
00:06:43,361 --> 00:06:45,571
You're doing a background check
on Lily Cruz?

138
00:06:45,655 --> 00:06:47,740
[tense music playing]

139
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:52,954
Do you think he's right about
Lily Cruz's real identity?

140
00:06:53,037 --> 00:06:56,332
It doesn't matter if he is, Emilia.

141
00:06:56,415 --> 00:06:58,251
Or whether Lily's a friend or a foe.

142
00:06:58,334 --> 00:07:01,754
Because, at the end of the day,
you've got the upper hand.

143
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:04,799
You just have to be aligned
with the right people.

144
00:07:04,882 --> 00:07:06,134
And that's me.

145
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:08,636
So you're saying…

146
00:07:08,719 --> 00:07:09,887
What I'm saying,

147
00:07:09,971 --> 00:07:12,306
is that I'll take care of Lily Cruz.

148
00:07:12,390 --> 00:07:13,724
I'll keep an eye on her.

149
00:07:13,808 --> 00:07:16,018
You focus on yourself.

150
00:07:16,102 --> 00:07:18,020
People are starting to notice
how Lily Cruz

151
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:19,814
has stressed you out.

152
00:07:19,897 --> 00:07:22,442
And that won't be good
for Arnaldo's campaign.

153
00:07:23,151 --> 00:07:24,318
Think about it.

154
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:29,031
Speaking of my future husband,
I'm going to his room.

155
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:30,575
Excuse me.

156
00:07:30,658 --> 00:07:31,784
Okay.

157
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:40,501
Madam, someone sent you these.

158
00:07:45,965 --> 00:07:48,634
What are you looking at?! Leave! Go!

159
00:07:50,261 --> 00:07:51,554
So nosy!

160
00:07:52,221 --> 00:07:57,685
[tense music playing]

161
00:07:57,768 --> 00:07:59,437
[chuckles]

162
00:08:03,524 --> 00:08:04,942
[giggles]

163
00:08:05,735 --> 00:08:07,195
Oh, Jaguar.

164
00:08:11,866 --> 00:08:14,285
Everyone, look!
Another point for Team Diego.

165
00:08:14,368 --> 00:08:15,703
-That's right!
-Yeah!

166
00:08:15,786 --> 00:08:19,373
-[cheering]
-[applause]

167
00:08:19,457 --> 00:08:22,835
My Diego is just that good!

168
00:08:22,919 --> 00:08:24,504
That's how it is

169
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:27,465
when one is sincere about serving others,

170
00:08:27,548 --> 00:08:30,009
and when one has no hidden agenda.

171
00:08:30,635 --> 00:08:33,763
You'll know he's sincere.
It'll come out naturally!

172
00:08:33,846 --> 00:08:37,934
That just proves that
experience isn't enough

173
00:08:38,017 --> 00:08:41,646
to dictate who a leader is supposed to be.

174
00:08:41,729 --> 00:08:42,772
-That's right!
-Correct!

175
00:08:42,855 --> 00:08:45,441
Mayor Arnaldo may be experienced,

176
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:47,902
but he's spent most of his term
making others suffer.

177
00:08:47,985 --> 00:08:49,320
-That's true.
-Right?

178
00:08:49,403 --> 00:08:50,988
-Right you are, Lily.
-Exactly.

179
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:53,449
Diego, congratulations again!

180
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,743
But we still have to be careful, though.

181
00:08:55,826 --> 00:08:59,372
The Ardientes won't give up that easily.

182
00:08:59,455 --> 00:09:04,043
They'll do everything
to make themselves look good.

183
00:09:04,126 --> 00:09:07,505
Remember the peace agreement
and the press conference?

184
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:09,966
[Marlon] Just like Arnaldo
and Ivy Aguas' wedding

185
00:09:10,049 --> 00:09:12,260
being held in the middle
of the campaign period.

186
00:09:12,343 --> 00:09:15,221
I'm sure it's a gimmick to get more votes!

187
00:09:15,304 --> 00:09:18,391
I don't even understand how that Ivy Aguas

188
00:09:18,474 --> 00:09:20,810
became so close with the Ardientes.

189
00:09:20,893 --> 00:09:25,022
I remember how she and Diego
used to be so close!

190
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:26,983
I don't get it, either!

191
00:09:27,066 --> 00:09:29,402
It's too bad they grew apart.

192
00:09:29,485 --> 00:09:31,946
But, you know what, I'm sure the Ardientes

193
00:09:32,029 --> 00:09:36,701
are going to use Ivy
in every gimmick they've got.

194
00:09:36,784 --> 00:09:40,329
[unsettling music playing]

195
00:09:44,125 --> 00:09:48,129
You know, someone's really
messing up my son's head.

196
00:09:48,212 --> 00:09:52,425
I don't know if it's that
Ivy Aguas or Lily Cruz.

197
00:09:52,508 --> 00:09:54,260
I really have to find out.

198
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:58,389
I know we can't trust
Ivy Aguas completely.

199
00:09:58,764 --> 00:10:00,600
But I'm just concerned, Emilia.

200
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:04,729
What if Arnaldo really has a problem?

201
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:06,105
Maybe he is…

202
00:10:06,188 --> 00:10:07,523
What problem?

203
00:10:08,524 --> 00:10:11,569
Are you trying to say that
Arnaldo is sick in the head?

204
00:10:11,652 --> 00:10:13,946
-Of course not.
-Are you implying that?

205
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:17,158
How dare you say that about your own son?

206
00:10:18,784 --> 00:10:19,827
All right. I'm sorry.

207
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:22,038
But what are you going to do now?

208
00:10:22,121 --> 00:10:23,122
What's your plan?

209
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:27,543
Well, somewhere, someone is laughing

210
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:29,378
and I have to stop it.

211
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:32,548
[tense music playing]

212
00:10:35,092 --> 00:10:37,470
Nice flowers there. You bought them?

213
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:41,223
No.

214
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:43,267
Who gave it to you?

215
00:10:43,893 --> 00:10:45,770
Someone who's very special.

216
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:47,229
-[Raul scoffs]
-Someone who knows…

217
00:10:47,313 --> 00:10:50,358
how to appreciate me and values me.

218
00:10:50,441 --> 00:10:51,901
Do you have a problem with that?

219
00:10:51,984 --> 00:10:54,570
No, but I'm sure Jaguar sent you that.

220
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:58,824
If I see that bastard,
I'll be sure to break his mask

221
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:00,451
and his face too. You'll see.

222
00:11:00,534 --> 00:11:01,744
And so?

223
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:04,622
At least Jaguar gives me flowers.

224
00:11:04,705 --> 00:11:05,706
Unlike you,

225
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:08,209
who can't even give me
a nice funeral wreath!

226
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:11,587
Here we go again.

227
00:11:17,718 --> 00:11:23,307
[unsettling music playing]

228
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:41,450
[muffled screams]

229
00:11:50,751 --> 00:11:55,172
[unsettling music playing]

230
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:59,093
[heavy breathing]

231
00:12:00,052 --> 00:12:01,429
No!

232
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:03,097
No!

233
00:12:03,514 --> 00:12:06,976
No! No! No!

234
00:12:07,435 --> 00:12:08,269
No!

235
00:12:08,352 --> 00:12:12,231
[Arnaldo screaming]

236
00:12:12,314 --> 00:12:14,108
[sobbing]

237
00:12:14,191 --> 00:12:18,863
[Arnaldo screaming]

238
00:12:18,946 --> 00:12:22,825
[screaming]

239
00:12:22,908 --> 00:12:24,493
Make it stop!

240
00:12:24,577 --> 00:12:25,870
Please!

241
00:12:25,953 --> 00:12:27,788
Please stop!

242
00:12:28,122 --> 00:12:29,748
Please make it stop!

243
00:12:30,332 --> 00:12:31,667
Stop it!

244
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:34,003
Please!

245
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,589
Please, stop!

246
00:12:36,672 --> 00:12:37,673
Hon?!

247
00:12:37,756 --> 00:12:39,508
-Hon? Hon!
-Make it stop!

248
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:41,427
-Hon, look at me!
-Please make it stop.

249
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:42,678
-Shh.
-Stop it!

250
00:12:42,761 --> 00:12:43,804
-Please!
-Hon!

251
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:44,889
Hon, calm down!

252
00:12:44,972 --> 00:12:46,515
Make it stop!

253
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:48,517
-Hon, I'm here!
-Make it stop!

254
00:12:48,601 --> 00:12:51,312
-[Arnaldo screaming]
-[Julio sobbing]

255
00:12:51,395 --> 00:12:52,396
<i>-Stop it!</i>
<i>-Hon!</i>

256
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,689
<i>-Make it stop!</i>
<i>-Hon, be strong!</i>

257
00:12:53,772 --> 00:12:55,483
-<i>Make it stop!</i>
-Why?

258
00:12:55,566 --> 00:12:56,859
-<i>Stop!</i>
-Why?!

259
00:12:57,943 --> 00:12:59,695
-<i>Make it stop!</i>
-Why?!

260
00:12:59,778 --> 00:13:01,489
[Arnaldo screaming]

261
00:13:01,947 --> 00:13:03,365
Make it stop! [sobbing]

262
00:13:03,449 --> 00:13:04,909
[Ivy's breath hitches]

263
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:08,787
<i>Who did this to you?!</i>

264
00:13:10,206 --> 00:13:13,125
<i>Tell me!</i>

265
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:18,547
[Arnaldo wailing]

266
00:13:19,048 --> 00:13:20,341
-Make it stop!
-Hon!

267
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:21,509
Make it stop!

268
00:13:21,842 --> 00:13:23,177
-Make what stop.
-What do you mean?

269
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:25,012
-Make it stop!
-What?

270
00:13:25,095 --> 00:13:26,263
Please!

271
00:13:26,347 --> 00:13:28,432
Stop it!

272
00:13:29,266 --> 00:13:30,559
[Arnaldo continues wailing]

273
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:31,769
Hon, hon!

274
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:33,687
-Stop it!
-Hon…

275
00:13:33,771 --> 00:13:35,814
What are you seeing?

276
00:13:36,899 --> 00:13:38,317
Why?

277
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:41,612
-[stifled cries]
-[faint screaming]

278
00:13:42,112 --> 00:13:43,239
No.

279
00:13:44,573 --> 00:13:45,533
No…

280
00:13:45,616 --> 00:13:46,617
No!

281
00:13:47,701 --> 00:13:49,119
Not him. Not him!

282
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:50,246
No!

283
00:13:52,665 --> 00:13:54,083
-Hon.
-[Arnaldo crying]

284
00:13:54,166 --> 00:13:56,627
-Hon, enough.
-Stop it!

285
00:13:56,710 --> 00:14:00,673
[uncontrollable screaming]

286
00:14:00,756 --> 00:14:02,174
[Arnaldo] Please, stop!

287
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:07,888
Ivy?

288
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:09,014
Shh.

289
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:10,641
What was that sound?

290
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:12,351
Huh?

291
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:16,105
What sound?

292
00:14:16,438 --> 00:14:19,942
I heard him shouting. It was so loud.

293
00:14:20,025 --> 00:14:21,193
Shouting?

294
00:14:23,362 --> 00:14:25,739
Arnaldo's been sleeping
this whole time, Emilia.

295
00:14:25,823 --> 00:14:27,658
Maybe you were dreaming.

296
00:14:29,326 --> 00:14:30,661
Hmm.

297
00:14:30,744 --> 00:14:31,871
-Okay.
-All right.

298
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:33,622
-Go back to bed.
-Good night.

299
00:14:34,832 --> 00:14:36,083
Good night.

300
00:14:38,794 --> 00:14:39,795
[door closes]

301
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:48,804
[dark music playing]

302
00:15:09,283 --> 00:15:11,243
Are these the places
we haven't visited yet?

303
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:12,411
Yes, ma'am.

304
00:15:12,494 --> 00:15:14,330
-Ah, okay.
-[phone ringing]

305
00:15:14,413 --> 00:15:15,789
Excuse me.

306
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:23,088
Hello? Lily, sweetie?

307
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:24,214
Mom?

308
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:26,800
[Camia sighs] <i>How are you there?</i>

309
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:28,594
Are you at the Ardientes'?

310
00:15:30,054 --> 00:15:31,680
Yes, Mom. I'm here.

311
00:15:32,932 --> 00:15:34,183
I miss you so much.

312
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,311
Mom, I miss you too.

313
00:15:38,103 --> 00:15:40,189
I miss you so much.

314
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:42,024
<i>So much, Mom.</i>

315
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:45,319
Lily, about what happened to Arnaldo

316
00:15:45,402 --> 00:15:47,154
during the debate earlier…

317
00:15:47,571 --> 00:15:48,781
<i>Did you do that?</i>

318
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:51,867
That was all me.

319
00:15:53,118 --> 00:15:54,286
Please be careful, okay?

320
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:57,706
If there's one thing
I don't want to happen,

321
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:59,166
it's you being caught up in danger.

322
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:01,585
Thank you, Mom.

323
00:16:01,961 --> 00:16:03,629
But that won't ever happen.

324
00:16:04,171 --> 00:16:05,673
<i>I'm doing fine, Mom.</i>

325
00:16:06,465 --> 00:16:10,219
If you could only see Arnaldo…

326
00:16:11,136 --> 00:16:12,221
[snickers]

327
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:17,142
All my plans are about to unfold.

328
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:18,727
<i>It's just a matter of time.</i>

329
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:20,354
It's so close now.

330
00:16:21,438 --> 00:16:23,023
What do you mean by that?

331
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:29,154
Just always be careful, okay?

332
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:31,573
I will, Mom. I promise.

333
00:16:31,949 --> 00:16:33,534
I'll always be careful.

334
00:16:34,159 --> 00:16:35,160
Bye, Lily.

335
00:16:36,745 --> 00:16:41,375
[unsettling music playing]

336
00:16:54,471 --> 00:16:55,889
Diego, congratulations.

337
00:16:55,973 --> 00:16:57,558
You did great during the debate.

338
00:16:58,017 --> 00:16:59,727
You outwitted Arnaldo.

339
00:17:03,313 --> 00:17:04,523
Thank you.

340
00:17:04,606 --> 00:17:07,776
[soft music playing]

341
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:10,070
How are you?

342
00:17:10,779 --> 00:17:11,947
Aren't you having a hard time?

343
00:17:14,158 --> 00:17:15,784
When you faced Emilia…

344
00:17:16,368 --> 00:17:19,246
you convinced her
that you really are Lily Cruz.

345
00:17:21,623 --> 00:17:23,876
When Lily and I were kids,

346
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:26,503
she was like my big sister.

347
00:17:28,172 --> 00:17:29,965
She was my best friend.

348
00:17:30,799 --> 00:17:35,012
She'd even prioritize my
welfare and Jepoy's over hers.

349
00:17:36,638 --> 00:17:38,766
Diego, this is the only way
for me to repay her

350
00:17:38,849 --> 00:17:40,809
for all the sacrifices she made for us.

351
00:17:40,893 --> 00:17:43,437
I'm only doing what's right.

352
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:46,523
This is for Lily and Aunt Carlotta's sake.

353
00:17:51,028 --> 00:17:52,154
[Diego] Anna, thank you very much.

354
00:17:52,237 --> 00:17:55,115
Thank you for helping Ivy in her mission.

355
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:56,784
And I assure you…

356
00:17:58,744 --> 00:18:00,746
I'll always be here to protect you.

357
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:04,541
Just like I promised to Ivy.

358
00:18:05,626 --> 00:18:10,255
[soft guitar music playing]

359
00:18:20,891 --> 00:18:25,896
[phone ringing]

360
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:29,817
-Diego?
-Ivy?

361
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:32,319
Diego, we need to talk.

362
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:33,904
Okay.

363
00:18:38,826 --> 00:18:40,828
Anna, I need to go.

364
00:18:40,911 --> 00:18:41,912
To Ivy, right?

365
00:18:43,872 --> 00:18:46,708
Okay. Be careful, all right?
And tell her I said hi.

366
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:48,544
Okay.

367
00:18:59,304 --> 00:19:00,722
Hey, Jepoy.

368
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:01,932
Anna, I'll go inside.

369
00:19:02,015 --> 00:19:03,100
Wait. Hold on.

370
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:04,852
I didn't see you all day,

371
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:06,812
and you won't even talk to me?

372
00:19:06,895 --> 00:19:08,063
Where have you been?

373
00:19:11,191 --> 00:19:12,734
Have you talked to Ivy yet?

374
00:19:14,027 --> 00:19:15,028
Mm-hm.

375
00:19:15,863 --> 00:19:18,782
Well, are you still upset

376
00:19:18,866 --> 00:19:20,826
because she's going to marry Arnaldo?

377
00:19:21,827 --> 00:19:23,036
[sighs]

378
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:24,163
Anna…

379
00:19:25,372 --> 00:19:27,583
I can't stop Ivy's plans.

380
00:19:29,459 --> 00:19:31,837
I'm just figuring out
another way to help her.

381
00:19:32,754 --> 00:19:33,755
All right?

382
00:19:36,425 --> 00:19:37,593
Get some rest, hmm?

383
00:19:37,676 --> 00:19:38,844
Okay.

384
00:19:52,691 --> 00:19:53,901
-Ivy.
-Diego.

385
00:19:55,110 --> 00:19:56,236
How are you?

386
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:57,529
I'm okay.

387
00:19:58,322 --> 00:19:59,740
Congratulations.

388
00:19:59,823 --> 00:20:01,742
You did great at the debate.

389
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:04,703
Thank you for your support.

390
00:20:05,704 --> 00:20:07,456
Whatever happened to Arnaldo…

391
00:20:08,248 --> 00:20:09,541
I know you were behind it.

392
00:20:12,211 --> 00:20:14,588
Ivy, what you're doing is dangerous.

393
00:20:15,464 --> 00:20:16,590
Be careful.

394
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:19,218
Thank you, Diego.

395
00:20:20,802 --> 00:20:22,095
I am being cautious.

396
00:20:23,305 --> 00:20:24,806
Slowly, but surely…

397
00:20:25,849 --> 00:20:28,810
my plans are unfolding.

398
00:20:29,728 --> 00:20:31,271
But this isn't the end of it.

399
00:20:32,439 --> 00:20:33,941
What more will you do?

400
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:41,865
[unsettling music playing]

401
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:52,167
[dark music playing]

402
00:21:01,969 --> 00:21:03,428
Good morning, hon!

403
00:21:04,054 --> 00:21:05,305
I'm glad you're awake now.

404
00:21:06,807 --> 00:21:09,351
Here, I made you breakfast.

405
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:11,770
How did you sleep?

406
00:21:12,771 --> 00:21:13,855
Hon?

407
00:21:16,984 --> 00:21:18,193
Hon.

408
00:21:19,444 --> 00:21:20,487
Did you…

409
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:23,740
Did you see something there last night?

410
00:21:26,243 --> 00:21:27,202
-Up there.
-Where?

411
00:21:27,286 --> 00:21:29,705
Up there, it was hanging up there.

412
00:21:29,788 --> 00:21:31,248
Up there on the ceiling.

413
00:21:31,331 --> 00:21:33,375
Something hanging from the ceiling?

414
00:21:33,458 --> 00:21:34,710
Yeah, up there.

415
00:21:36,253 --> 00:21:37,337
I think…

416
00:21:38,255 --> 00:21:39,756
I think it looked like…

417
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:47,222
It looked like who?

418
00:21:49,391 --> 00:21:51,310
Who did it look like, hon?

419
00:21:54,229 --> 00:21:55,814
Who did you see?

420
00:21:59,484 --> 00:22:00,694
Who?

421
00:22:03,405 --> 00:22:04,531
Uh…

422
00:22:07,701 --> 00:22:09,077
[sighs]

423
00:22:10,078 --> 00:22:11,121
[chuckles]

424
00:22:11,204 --> 00:22:13,790
Hon, maybe you just had a nightmare.

425
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:16,668
Just forget about it.

426
00:22:17,878 --> 00:22:19,588
Don't mind it, hon.

427
00:22:19,671 --> 00:22:22,049
Let's just get ready
for your campaign later.

428
00:22:22,632 --> 00:22:24,176
So, eat your breakfast.

429
00:22:24,259 --> 00:22:25,802
I'll just go to the restroom.

430
00:22:25,886 --> 00:22:26,970
Okay?

431
00:22:30,849 --> 00:22:32,225
Good morning.

432
00:22:40,317 --> 00:22:47,032
[ominous music playing]

433
00:22:47,115 --> 00:22:51,787
[phone ringing]

434
00:22:52,829 --> 00:22:53,789
Hello?

435
00:22:53,872 --> 00:22:56,166
Prepare 20 million pesos…

436
00:22:56,249 --> 00:22:59,044
<i>Arnaldo Ardiente.</i>

437
00:22:59,127 --> 00:23:00,712
<i>Do it if you don't want</i>

438
00:23:00,796 --> 00:23:03,590
<i>your dirty secrets to be exposed.</i>

439
00:23:03,673 --> 00:23:05,884
Twenty million pesos? Are you crazy?

440
00:23:05,967 --> 00:23:06,760
<i>If you're threatening me…</i>

441
00:23:06,843 --> 00:23:08,512
I'm not afraid of you.

442
00:23:08,595 --> 00:23:10,931
If you're joking, it's not even funny.

443
00:23:11,014 --> 00:23:12,891
Twenty million pesos, Mayor.

444
00:23:13,433 --> 00:23:14,684
<i>Bring it to the plaza…</i>

445
00:23:14,768 --> 00:23:16,436
within an hour.

446
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,355
How about I trace this call?

447
00:23:18,730 --> 00:23:19,773
<i>I'll hunt you down…</i>

448
00:23:19,856 --> 00:23:21,650
and kill you. How's that sound?

449
00:23:21,733 --> 00:23:23,819
[sinister laughter]

450
00:23:24,152 --> 00:23:25,654
You'll regret this.

451
00:23:26,404 --> 00:23:27,823
-I will kill--
-[line drops]

452
00:23:27,906 --> 00:23:29,074
Hello?

453
00:23:31,409 --> 00:23:32,577
Hello?!

454
00:23:33,578 --> 00:23:34,871
-Hell--
-[door opening]

455
00:23:34,955 --> 00:23:36,248
Hon?

456
00:23:36,915 --> 00:23:38,542
Who were you talking to?

457
00:23:41,628 --> 00:23:42,587
My staff.

458
00:23:42,671 --> 00:23:45,090
You need more bodyguards for
our grassroots project later.

459
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:46,758
Oh.

460
00:23:46,842 --> 00:23:48,135
Thanks, hon.

461
00:23:49,427 --> 00:23:50,470
Anyway…

462
00:23:51,888 --> 00:23:53,807
It's hot, hon. I'll go take a shower.

463
00:23:54,641 --> 00:23:55,725
Okay?

464
00:24:00,355 --> 00:24:06,736
[tense music playing]

465
00:24:24,212 --> 00:24:28,717
[tense music playing]

466
00:24:46,484 --> 00:24:47,986
Wanna join, hon?

467
00:25:08,548 --> 00:25:12,344
Well, we'll see Diego again
at the campaign later.

468
00:25:12,677 --> 00:25:14,721
So, I want you to, uh…

469
00:25:16,056 --> 00:25:19,351
[shower running]

470
00:25:19,434 --> 00:25:20,518
[glass breaking]

471
00:25:20,602 --> 00:25:23,396
[ominous music playing]

472
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:24,773
[mouthing] Ivy?

473
00:25:24,856 --> 00:25:28,526
[shower running]

474
00:25:28,610 --> 00:25:29,694
Ivy?

475
00:25:29,778 --> 00:25:31,321
[shower running]

476
00:25:31,404 --> 00:25:32,197
Ivy?

477
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:33,114
[ominous music]

478
00:25:33,198 --> 00:25:34,282
[shower running]

479
00:25:34,366 --> 00:25:35,617
Ivy?

480
00:25:37,911 --> 00:25:43,041
-[shower running]
-[ominous music playing]

481
00:25:47,504 --> 00:25:50,465
[ominous music continues]

482
00:25:54,302 --> 00:25:58,390
[shower continues running]

483
00:25:58,473 --> 00:26:03,645
[phone ringing]

484
00:26:06,022 --> 00:26:07,232
Where's Ivy?

485
00:26:07,315 --> 00:26:08,692
[man] <i>I warned you, didn't I?</i>

486
00:26:08,775 --> 00:26:10,151
You will regret this.

487
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:11,319
Where's Ivy?!

488
00:26:11,403 --> 00:26:13,571
[sinister laughter]

489
00:26:13,655 --> 00:26:14,739
<i>Relax.</i>

490
00:26:15,282 --> 00:26:16,658
<i>You will get back…</i>

491
00:26:16,741 --> 00:26:19,828
what I took if you do as I say.

492
00:26:20,704 --> 00:26:22,122
<i>But if you don't…</i>

493
00:26:22,205 --> 00:26:26,835
Ivy Aguas will die.

494
00:26:26,918 --> 00:26:28,586
You bastard!

495
00:26:28,670 --> 00:26:32,716
[sinister laughter]

496
00:26:34,843 --> 00:26:36,219
[mouthing] I will kill you.

497
00:26:39,889 --> 00:26:40,932
Diego.

498
00:26:43,059 --> 00:26:44,644
Have you met with Lily yet?

499
00:26:45,145 --> 00:26:46,479
We talked earlier.

500
00:26:46,563 --> 00:26:49,524
She told me she had a plan
to corner Arnaldo.

501
00:26:49,941 --> 00:26:51,234
Do you know anything about this?

502
00:26:52,027 --> 00:26:53,194
Yes, Auntie.

503
00:26:53,278 --> 00:26:55,739
The last time we spoke, she told me…

504
00:26:56,114 --> 00:26:57,824
that she'd need my help.

505
00:26:58,616 --> 00:26:59,743
Is that so?

506
00:27:00,660 --> 00:27:01,786
I hope for the best.

507
00:27:02,662 --> 00:27:06,916
Diego, I fear something bad
might happen to her.

508
00:27:07,834 --> 00:27:09,044
Auntie, don't worry.

509
00:27:09,127 --> 00:27:10,754
I'll always remind her.

510
00:27:12,088 --> 00:27:15,800
[unsettling music playing]

511
00:27:20,764 --> 00:27:21,806
Ivy.

512
00:27:21,890 --> 00:27:24,017
[mumbling] Ivy… Where is Ivy?

513
00:27:24,100 --> 00:27:26,227
Ivy… Ivy… Ivy…

514
00:27:26,770 --> 00:27:28,313
[mysterious caller] <i>You'll regret this.</i>

515
00:27:30,023 --> 00:27:31,149
[Ivy] <i>I'll just go to the restroom.</i>

516
00:27:31,232 --> 00:27:32,525
<i>Good morning.</i>

517
00:27:32,609 --> 00:27:33,735
Ivy.

518
00:27:33,818 --> 00:27:37,280
[suspenseful music playing]

519
00:27:37,364 --> 00:27:38,865
<i>Wanna join me, hon?</i>

520
00:27:40,867 --> 00:27:43,828
<i>Well, we'll see Diego again</i>
<i>at the campaign.</i>

521
00:27:45,455 --> 00:27:46,664
Ivy…

522
00:27:46,748 --> 00:27:48,666
Ivy, where are you?

523
00:27:50,377 --> 00:27:51,336
<i>Ivy?</i>

524
00:27:52,253 --> 00:27:53,838
[panting]

525
00:27:53,922 --> 00:27:55,090
Ivy.

526
00:27:55,173 --> 00:27:56,841
[panicked breathing]

527
00:27:56,925 --> 00:27:58,385
[groans]

528
00:27:58,468 --> 00:27:59,344
<i>You'll regret this.</i>

529
00:27:59,427 --> 00:28:00,678
<i>It's hot, hon. I'll go take a shower.</i>

530
00:28:00,762 --> 00:28:02,180
<i>-Twenty million pesos, Mayor.</i>
<i>-Wanna join me, hon?</i>

531
00:28:02,263 --> 00:28:05,767
-[sinister laughter]
-<i>Ivy Aguas will die.</i>

532
00:28:05,850 --> 00:28:08,103
Ivy… Ivy…

533
00:28:10,897 --> 00:28:11,898
Thank you.

534
00:28:12,899 --> 00:28:14,526
Ivy? Ivy?

535
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:16,444
-Ivy?
-Hey!

536
00:28:16,528 --> 00:28:17,570
Arnaldo!

537
00:28:18,029 --> 00:28:19,781
My grandson! Come here.

538
00:28:20,323 --> 00:28:22,325
Join me for breakfast.

539
00:28:22,409 --> 00:28:23,451
Come on!

540
00:28:25,036 --> 00:28:26,287
I have things to tell you.

541
00:28:26,371 --> 00:28:27,163
Oh?

542
00:28:28,081 --> 00:28:29,791
Did you just wake up?

543
00:28:30,875 --> 00:28:32,460
You haven't even showered. Sit down.

544
00:28:32,544 --> 00:28:33,753
Sit down!

545
00:28:34,838 --> 00:28:35,630
Come on.

546
00:28:35,713 --> 00:28:36,881
-[Arnaldo coughs]
-Uh…

547
00:28:38,049 --> 00:28:39,551
Is there any problem?

548
00:28:40,719 --> 00:28:42,387
-Problem?
-Yeah.

549
00:28:42,470 --> 00:28:44,389
-Nothing.
-Okay.

550
00:28:44,472 --> 00:28:47,225
-Nothing.
-Anyway, as I was telling you.

551
00:28:47,308 --> 00:28:50,228
You know, I realized, after we spoke,

552
00:28:50,311 --> 00:28:51,980
I realized you were right.

553
00:28:52,063 --> 00:28:54,190
You were right, Arnaldo.

554
00:28:54,274 --> 00:28:56,443
We can fix this situation.

555
00:28:57,277 --> 00:29:00,905
To ensure your win…

556
00:29:00,989 --> 00:29:02,282
You have to--

557
00:29:02,365 --> 00:29:04,117
Arnaldo, listen to me!

558
00:29:04,451 --> 00:29:06,745
You have to push through with the wedding.

559
00:29:06,828 --> 00:29:08,037
-Okay.
-You know what…

560
00:29:08,121 --> 00:29:09,622
With all the preparations,

561
00:29:09,706 --> 00:29:13,126
in a couple of weeks, you can get married.

562
00:29:13,209 --> 00:29:15,587
And you know how Filipinos are.

563
00:29:15,670 --> 00:29:18,757
You know how we are! We're romantic!

564
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:20,550
Filipinos adore love stories!

565
00:29:20,633 --> 00:29:22,761
They love fairy tales and happy endings!

566
00:29:22,844 --> 00:29:25,096
And people who are getting married

567
00:29:25,180 --> 00:29:28,641
are perceived to be better
at things they do.

568
00:29:28,725 --> 00:29:32,312
They're perceived to be
more efficient at work.

569
00:29:32,395 --> 00:29:33,938
And if that's how the people think,

570
00:29:34,022 --> 00:29:35,774
they're certainly going to vote for you!

571
00:29:35,857 --> 00:29:37,525
We are going to win this battle.

572
00:29:37,609 --> 00:29:41,654
Now, join me here.
We have a wedding to plan.

573
00:29:41,738 --> 00:29:43,198
I mean, not just a wedding, but--

574
00:29:43,281 --> 00:29:44,699
Let's plan out every detail!

575
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:49,204
You know what?
You better call Ivy here too!

576
00:29:49,287 --> 00:29:51,873
She needs to be here for this!

577
00:29:52,707 --> 00:29:54,209
This is going to be good.

578
00:29:55,752 --> 00:29:56,753
Ivy…

579
00:29:56,836 --> 00:29:58,254
Yeah, call her.

580
00:29:59,547 --> 00:30:00,632
She went home.

581
00:30:01,299 --> 00:30:02,801
She… She went home?

582
00:30:03,343 --> 00:30:05,261
She went home. I'll go get her.

583
00:30:05,345 --> 00:30:06,763
You know, that's good.

584
00:30:06,846 --> 00:30:08,056
All right. You go do that.

585
00:30:08,139 --> 00:30:10,141
Tell her we're planning something.

586
00:30:10,225 --> 00:30:11,726
I'll wait. I'll wait.

587
00:30:13,061 --> 00:30:14,187
It's okay.

588
00:30:14,854 --> 00:30:18,817
[unsettling music playing]

589
00:30:36,042 --> 00:30:37,085
Guard!

590
00:30:38,002 --> 00:30:39,379
Did you see anyone here?

591
00:30:39,462 --> 00:30:40,797
Anyone suspicious?

592
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:41,923
Someone you don't know?

593
00:30:42,006 --> 00:30:43,591
No, Mayor. I didn't see anyone.

594
00:30:44,384 --> 00:30:45,343
How about Ivy?

595
00:30:45,426 --> 00:30:47,679
Did you see her come out?
Did you see her leave?

596
00:30:47,762 --> 00:30:49,973
-I didn't, sir.
-What are we paying you for?!

597
00:30:50,056 --> 00:30:53,059
To just stand there and flirt
with all the maids?!

598
00:30:54,018 --> 00:30:55,520
You're useless! Out of the way!

599
00:30:59,983 --> 00:31:04,821
-[car engine revving]
-[unsettling music playing]

600
00:31:21,379 --> 00:31:23,131
[tires screeching]

601
00:31:24,632 --> 00:31:27,552
Watch where you're going!
You could've killed us!

602
00:31:29,095 --> 00:31:34,309
[unsettling music playing]

603
00:31:47,655 --> 00:31:51,451
[unsettling music playing]

604
00:31:55,997 --> 00:31:57,540
<i>Mayor Arnaldo!</i>

605
00:32:09,802 --> 00:32:12,180
Papa, where is Arnaldo?

606
00:32:12,263 --> 00:32:13,932
I can't have a family meeting

607
00:32:14,015 --> 00:32:16,267
without the future governor.

608
00:32:18,561 --> 00:32:20,813
Arnaldo is with Ivy.

609
00:32:21,564 --> 00:32:22,607
By the way…

610
00:32:23,232 --> 00:32:25,234
Didn't I tell you…

611
00:32:26,361 --> 00:32:28,237
to kill Jaguar?

612
00:32:28,321 --> 00:32:30,114
[tense music playing]

613
00:32:30,198 --> 00:32:31,282
What happened?

614
00:32:31,366 --> 00:32:32,742
Have you done the deed yet?

615
00:32:34,619 --> 00:32:35,828
No, Papa.

616
00:32:37,830 --> 00:32:42,043
You know, we have a real problem at hand.

617
00:32:42,627 --> 00:32:47,048
I mean, now that the
campaign is ongoing, and…

618
00:32:47,757 --> 00:32:49,509
Diego is leading…

619
00:32:50,343 --> 00:32:52,345
I cannot afford…

620
00:32:53,096 --> 00:32:59,268
to let Jaguar and Diego combine forces.

621
00:32:59,352 --> 00:33:01,104
That cannot be.

622
00:33:02,522 --> 00:33:04,774
So, what do you think we should do?

623
00:33:05,358 --> 00:33:08,403
If Emilia couldn't kill Jaguar,

624
00:33:08,486 --> 00:33:10,613
then we should get him on our side.

625
00:33:11,072 --> 00:33:13,116
It's like making a deal with a devil.

626
00:33:13,199 --> 00:33:16,703
[tense music playing]

627
00:33:16,786 --> 00:33:19,914
There is only one devil in Ardiente.

628
00:33:21,165 --> 00:33:22,458
The rest are…

629
00:33:23,084 --> 00:33:28,089
pawns and spineless goody-goody gum drops.

630
00:33:29,424 --> 00:33:34,637
If Jaguar wants his syndicate to survive…

631
00:33:35,263 --> 00:33:38,641
I am the devil that he should worship.

632
00:33:38,725 --> 00:33:42,103
[tense music playing]

633
00:33:42,186 --> 00:33:43,312
Papa, what if…

634
00:33:43,855 --> 00:33:47,984
What if Jaguar doesn't agree?

635
00:33:49,318 --> 00:33:50,445
Well…

636
00:33:50,528 --> 00:33:54,407
He should be reminded
that he is just a jaguar…

637
00:33:55,158 --> 00:33:56,242
and I am a lion.

638
00:33:57,201 --> 00:33:59,454
And the lion is the king of the jungle.

639
00:34:00,204 --> 00:34:02,290
And I will eat him alive.

640
00:34:02,373 --> 00:34:08,046
[tense music playing]

641
00:34:16,721 --> 00:34:19,932
You know that you can't serve
two masters, Emilia.

642
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:22,727
Auntie, I'm not serving
either one of them.

643
00:34:23,352 --> 00:34:26,731
I just don't tell Papa
that I'm meeting with Jaguar.

644
00:34:26,814 --> 00:34:28,399
And same goes with Jaguar.

645
00:34:28,483 --> 00:34:31,069
I don't tell him
what Papa and I talk about.

646
00:34:31,152 --> 00:34:32,153
[Claire scoffs]

647
00:34:32,779 --> 00:34:34,280
So, you're playing safe?

648
00:34:34,989 --> 00:34:37,283
Well, you can say that.

649
00:34:37,784 --> 00:34:40,036
I'll go to whoever will win

650
00:34:40,119 --> 00:34:42,080
between Papa and Jaguar.

651
00:34:45,833 --> 00:34:47,752
[Rufo] <i>That old man has a lot of nerve.</i>

652
00:34:47,835 --> 00:34:50,129
Did he really expect you
to join forces with him?

653
00:34:51,798 --> 00:34:54,008
The Ardientes are going down, Jaguar.

654
00:34:55,635 --> 00:34:58,012
Did you see his grandson, the mayor?

655
00:34:58,679 --> 00:34:59,806
He walked out.

656
00:35:00,890 --> 00:35:01,766
He was shaken.

657
00:35:01,849 --> 00:35:03,059
How can he possibly win?

658
00:35:03,142 --> 00:35:04,811
Watch your tongue, Rufo.

659
00:35:04,894 --> 00:35:06,771
That's still my son we're talking about.

660
00:35:11,317 --> 00:35:12,276
But…

661
00:35:12,360 --> 00:35:13,778
between the two of them,

662
00:35:13,861 --> 00:35:15,446
who would you want to win?

663
00:35:16,030 --> 00:35:17,073
It's Diego, right?

664
00:35:17,448 --> 00:35:20,284
And yet he continues to reject your help.

665
00:35:21,369 --> 00:35:22,453
Jaguar…

666
00:35:22,537 --> 00:35:24,580
The Ardientes are
desperate to work with you.

667
00:35:24,664 --> 00:35:26,707
But Diego's group keeps pushing you away.

668
00:35:26,791 --> 00:35:27,875
What will you do?

669
00:35:28,334 --> 00:35:29,377
Where will you stand?

670
00:35:31,379 --> 00:35:33,881
Until a decision needs to be made…

671
00:35:35,466 --> 00:35:37,009
I don't have to worry about that.

672
00:35:37,093 --> 00:35:40,596
The only thing we should do
is get stronger.

673
00:35:41,430 --> 00:35:44,308
That Madrigal. We need him in our group.

674
00:35:45,184 --> 00:35:47,353
You should work on that.

675
00:35:47,436 --> 00:35:48,437
Do you understand?

676
00:35:49,564 --> 00:35:53,568
[tense music playing]

677
00:35:54,735 --> 00:35:56,237
We signed a peace agreement.

678
00:35:56,320 --> 00:35:59,157
Not a single one of
the Ardientes or their men

679
00:35:59,240 --> 00:36:01,534
can get past this line, do you understand?

680
00:36:01,617 --> 00:36:02,743
Yes, sir.

681
00:36:03,369 --> 00:36:04,495
Yes, sir.

682
00:36:04,579 --> 00:36:05,997
Carl, get into position.

683
00:36:12,295 --> 00:36:17,383
[ominous music playing]

684
00:36:22,638 --> 00:36:24,390
He's not one of the Ardientes, right?

685
00:36:24,473 --> 00:36:25,641
He works for Jaguar.

686
00:36:26,684 --> 00:36:27,810
Jaguar?

687
00:36:28,394 --> 00:36:31,814
[ominous music playing]

688
00:36:31,898 --> 00:36:34,525
Isn't that the group
fighting the Ardientes?

689
00:36:34,609 --> 00:36:36,110
You're right, Madrigal.

690
00:36:36,194 --> 00:36:37,653
They're a vicious group.

691
00:36:39,447 --> 00:36:40,656
Who's that?

692
00:36:40,740 --> 00:36:43,117
Jaguar's right-hand man. His name is Rufo.

693
00:36:44,619 --> 00:36:45,786
Rufo?

694
00:36:53,169 --> 00:36:55,004
Congressman, confirmed.

695
00:36:55,087 --> 00:36:57,632
Jaguar has been watching Diego's camp.

696
00:36:57,715 --> 00:37:01,344
Are those idiots
really going to join forces?!

697
00:37:01,427 --> 00:37:03,679
Do you mean to tell me that Jaguar

698
00:37:03,763 --> 00:37:06,807
and that snot-nosed Diego are teaming up?

699
00:37:06,891 --> 00:37:08,684
<i>What are you waiting for?</i>

700
00:37:08,768 --> 00:37:10,061
Bring me that man!

701
00:37:10,144 --> 00:37:11,145
<i>Yes, sir.</i>

702
00:37:13,439 --> 00:37:16,609
[ominous music playing]

703
00:37:16,692 --> 00:37:17,735
Let's go.

704
00:37:26,327 --> 00:37:27,912
Don't they work for the Ardientes?

705
00:37:34,001 --> 00:37:35,628
[grunts, groans]

706
00:37:35,711 --> 00:37:36,712
Don't!

707
00:37:36,796 --> 00:37:37,755
Lower your guns.

708
00:37:37,838 --> 00:37:38,631
Don't get involved.

709
00:37:38,714 --> 00:37:39,840
-[groans]
-Let him be.

710
00:37:39,924 --> 00:37:40,967
[grunts]

711
00:37:41,050 --> 00:37:42,426
-[grunts] Take him inside.
-Get in!

712
00:37:43,928 --> 00:37:45,012
Get in!

713
00:37:46,430 --> 00:37:51,519
[suspenseful music playing]

714
00:37:53,896 --> 00:37:55,523
Ivy? Ivy!

715
00:37:56,315 --> 00:37:57,358
Ivy!

716
00:37:57,441 --> 00:37:59,902
[unsettling music playing]

717
00:37:59,986 --> 00:38:01,404
Ivy? Ivy!

718
00:38:02,196 --> 00:38:03,239
Ivy?!

719
00:38:04,699 --> 00:38:05,783
Hey, Arnaldo!

720
00:38:07,243 --> 00:38:08,369
Ivy…

721
00:38:08,452 --> 00:38:09,870
Have you found anything?

722
00:38:09,954 --> 00:38:11,539
-Not yet, Mayor.
-Well, keep looking!

723
00:38:11,622 --> 00:38:13,374
-Keep looking!
-[whispers] Emilia…

724
00:38:13,457 --> 00:38:15,626
Hey! Arnaldo, what's going on?

725
00:38:16,419 --> 00:38:17,253
-Ivy…
-What?

726
00:38:17,336 --> 00:38:18,796
Ivy… Ivy…

727
00:38:18,879 --> 00:38:20,715
-No, no, no.
-Can you please tell us…

728
00:38:20,798 --> 00:38:22,383
-what's going on?
-No, no. Something--

729
00:38:22,466 --> 00:38:24,302
Hey! Can you--

730
00:38:24,385 --> 00:38:26,220
[stutters] Ivy…

731
00:38:26,304 --> 00:38:27,638
-Something…
-What?!

732
00:38:27,722 --> 00:38:29,348
-Something's happening.
-What going on with Ivy?

733
00:38:29,432 --> 00:38:30,433
Something's hap--

734
00:38:30,766 --> 00:38:34,437
[panting]

735
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:35,980
Are you back to your senses?

736
00:38:36,063 --> 00:38:39,734
-[unsettling music playing]
-[heavy breathing]

737
00:38:39,817 --> 00:38:41,027
Ivy.

738
00:38:41,110 --> 00:38:42,653
What's with Ivy?!

739
00:38:42,737 --> 00:38:44,655
Tell us what's bothering you!

740
00:38:44,739 --> 00:38:45,823
Arnaldo!

741
00:38:46,240 --> 00:38:48,075
Ivy… She is…

742
00:38:48,159 --> 00:38:50,411
She's what? Tell us! She's what?

743
00:38:50,494 --> 00:38:51,287
She's… uh--

744
00:38:51,370 --> 00:38:56,375
[phone ringing]

745
00:38:56,459 --> 00:38:57,209
Hello?

746
00:38:57,293 --> 00:38:59,503
Do you want to get Ivy Aguas back?

747
00:38:59,587 --> 00:39:01,422
Damn you! What do you want?!

748
00:39:01,505 --> 00:39:02,465
Hey, come on!

749
00:39:02,548 --> 00:39:04,216
Can you please tell us what's going on?

750
00:39:04,300 --> 00:39:05,760
<i>Face me by yourself.</i>

751
00:39:05,843 --> 00:39:06,886
Just you.

752
00:39:07,803 --> 00:39:10,389
<i>No Ardientes. No cops.</i>

753
00:39:11,349 --> 00:39:12,683
<i>No pesky media.</i>

754
00:39:13,017 --> 00:39:14,185
Or else…

755
00:39:14,977 --> 00:39:17,021
Ivy Aguas will die.

756
00:39:20,024 --> 00:39:21,233
Hey! Psst!

757
00:39:21,942 --> 00:39:22,985
What?

758
00:39:23,069 --> 00:39:24,403
Arnaldo.

759
00:39:24,487 --> 00:39:25,654
Arnaldo!

760
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:27,323
Did you see that?

761
00:39:27,406 --> 00:39:28,657
Emilia, something is wrong.

762
00:39:28,741 --> 00:39:30,159
What is happening again?

763
00:39:31,952 --> 00:39:33,704
[phone ringing]

764
00:39:34,288 --> 00:39:36,540
Listen to me. I'm the mayor of this town,

765
00:39:36,624 --> 00:39:38,959
and I will not be threatened by nobody.

766
00:39:39,043 --> 00:39:41,170
<i>For all I know, you don't even have Ivy.</i>

767
00:39:41,253 --> 00:39:43,381
But don't worry.
Now, you have my attention.

768
00:39:43,464 --> 00:39:45,841
I will track you down and kill you myself.

769
00:39:45,925 --> 00:39:47,009
Do you hear me? Huh?

770
00:39:47,093 --> 00:39:48,594
<i>I'll kill you!</i>

771
00:39:48,677 --> 00:39:49,762
-I'll kill--
-[line drops]

772
00:39:50,346 --> 00:39:51,389
[screams in frustration]

773
00:39:51,931 --> 00:39:52,973
[grumbles]

774
00:39:53,057 --> 00:39:54,266
No, no.

775
00:39:54,892 --> 00:39:56,852
[grumbling]

776
00:39:56,936 --> 00:40:01,607
[tense music playing]

777
00:40:01,941 --> 00:40:02,942
[phone chimes]

778
00:40:03,651 --> 00:40:08,406
[suspenseful music playing]

779
00:40:12,076 --> 00:40:13,911
[mysterious caller]
<i>Twenty million pesos, Mayor.</i>

780
00:40:13,994 --> 00:40:17,456
<i>Or else, Ivy Aguas will die.</i>

781
00:40:17,540 --> 00:40:22,086
[suspenseful music playing]

782
00:40:22,169 --> 00:40:23,671
No, no, no, no.

783
00:40:23,754 --> 00:40:27,258
[panicked breathing]

784
00:40:29,218 --> 00:40:30,469
Arnaldo?

785
00:40:31,303 --> 00:40:32,638
Hey, son!

786
00:40:33,013 --> 00:40:34,348
-What's going on?!
-Arnaldo!

787
00:40:35,933 --> 00:40:37,726
-Arnaldo!
-Arnaldo, hey!

788
00:40:37,810 --> 00:40:39,103
Tell me. What's going on?

789
00:40:39,186 --> 00:40:41,814
[tense music playing]

790
00:40:41,897 --> 00:40:42,982
Arnaldo.

791
00:40:44,066 --> 00:40:45,985
We are family, Arnaldo, okay?

792
00:40:46,569 --> 00:40:48,988
Whatever is bothering you, I'm sure…

793
00:40:49,613 --> 00:40:51,907
…your mother and your grandpa
can help you.

794
00:40:52,283 --> 00:40:54,201
We'll do something about it.

795
00:40:54,285 --> 00:40:55,369
-Yes!
-Okay?

796
00:40:55,828 --> 00:40:58,414
[mysterious caller]
<i>Face me by yourself. Just you.</i>

797
00:40:58,497 --> 00:41:00,666
<i>No Ardientes. No cops.</i>

798
00:41:01,125 --> 00:41:04,128
<i>Or else, Ivy Aguas will die.</i>

799
00:41:06,881 --> 00:41:08,924
Okay, uh… [clears throat]

800
00:41:11,260 --> 00:41:12,261
Uh…

801
00:41:14,972 --> 00:41:15,723
I'm okay.

802
00:41:15,806 --> 00:41:16,974
Huh?

803
00:41:17,433 --> 00:41:18,350
I'm okay.

804
00:41:18,434 --> 00:41:20,186
-Uh… Nothing's wrong.
-But you were just…

805
00:41:20,811 --> 00:41:22,771
You were almost hysterical earlier.

806
00:41:23,689 --> 00:41:24,982
What's happening, Arnaldo?

807
00:41:25,065 --> 00:41:26,525
Who were you talking to on the phone?

808
00:41:27,860 --> 00:41:28,903
Uh…

809
00:41:29,904 --> 00:41:32,156
I'm sorry, but that was
just a business partner.

810
00:41:32,239 --> 00:41:33,115
And…

811
00:41:33,199 --> 00:41:34,950
We had a little disagreement.

812
00:41:35,034 --> 00:41:36,702
But it's okay now.

813
00:41:36,785 --> 00:41:37,786
What?!

814
00:41:38,370 --> 00:41:41,165
All the while, you were
talking about business?

815
00:41:42,124 --> 00:41:43,209
Yes.

816
00:41:44,293 --> 00:41:45,711
Yes. Uh…

817
00:41:45,794 --> 00:41:46,962
So, excuse me.

818
00:41:47,046 --> 00:41:53,344
[unsettling music playing]

819
00:41:55,221 --> 00:41:56,430
Business?

820
00:41:58,224 --> 00:41:59,350
[sighs]

821
00:42:02,770 --> 00:42:04,855
-[grunting, panting]
-[shushes]

822
00:42:05,439 --> 00:42:06,732
Let him go.

823
00:42:06,815 --> 00:42:09,360
[tense music playing]

824
00:42:09,443 --> 00:42:11,445
Welcome, Rufo.

825
00:42:12,154 --> 00:42:13,197
Sit down.

826
00:42:13,864 --> 00:42:16,367
Would you like to have a drink?

827
00:42:16,742 --> 00:42:18,786
You don't have to do that, Congressman.

828
00:42:19,662 --> 00:42:22,081
You won't win me over
with your nice guy act.

829
00:42:22,164 --> 00:42:23,499
Act?

830
00:42:24,375 --> 00:42:25,459
You're mistaken, Rufo.

831
00:42:26,418 --> 00:42:28,671
I don't do pretensions.

832
00:42:28,754 --> 00:42:29,630
Actually…

833
00:42:29,713 --> 00:42:32,841
I am the most straightforward person

834
00:42:32,925 --> 00:42:34,802
you will meet in the world.

835
00:42:36,095 --> 00:42:37,763
Why did you bring me here?

836
00:42:38,847 --> 00:42:39,890
Well…

837
00:42:41,308 --> 00:42:44,645
I wanted to talk to Jaguar.

838
00:42:44,728 --> 00:42:45,854
[scoffs]

839
00:42:45,938 --> 00:42:48,566
I'd like to offer him a deal.

840
00:42:49,233 --> 00:42:50,359
But the thing is,

841
00:42:50,901 --> 00:42:52,361
I know he would never agree,

842
00:42:52,444 --> 00:42:55,781
knowing I would be the one talking to him.

843
00:42:56,699 --> 00:42:57,908
That's why I brought you here.

844
00:42:57,992 --> 00:42:58,909
Maybe…

845
00:42:59,493 --> 00:43:04,540
Maybe you can find a way
to make it happen.

846
00:43:05,791 --> 00:43:06,834
And…

847
00:43:06,917 --> 00:43:09,878
the way I see it, the
easiest way to do that

848
00:43:09,962 --> 00:43:11,839
would be to break Jaguar's trust.

849
00:43:11,922 --> 00:43:13,799
Try to destroy his will.

850
00:43:14,341 --> 00:43:16,468
Until eventually…

851
00:43:17,803 --> 00:43:20,097
he decides to reach out to me.

852
00:43:22,391 --> 00:43:23,934
Congressman.

853
00:43:24,018 --> 00:43:25,978
You're talking to the wrong man.

854
00:43:29,481 --> 00:43:32,276
[tense music playing]

855
00:43:32,359 --> 00:43:35,738
Like I said, Rufo…

856
00:43:37,114 --> 00:43:40,993
I am the most straightforward man

857
00:43:41,076 --> 00:43:42,786
you will ever meet in the world.

858
00:43:43,287 --> 00:43:44,371
Now…

859
00:43:47,750 --> 00:43:49,585
What is it going to be?

860
00:43:49,668 --> 00:43:53,881
[tense music playing]

861
00:44:17,905 --> 00:44:24,787
[ominous music playing]

862
00:44:34,630 --> 00:44:36,465
[mumbling] Plaza, plaza, plaza.

863
00:44:39,802 --> 00:44:46,308
[ominous music playing]

864
00:44:48,227 --> 00:44:49,353
[Clara] Please double-check it

865
00:44:49,436 --> 00:44:51,522
because the mayor needs this
by next week, okay?

866
00:44:51,605 --> 00:44:52,481
Yes, ma'am.

867
00:44:52,564 --> 00:44:53,899
[phone rings]

868
00:44:54,817 --> 00:44:56,068
[Clara] <i>Hello? Mayor?</i>

869
00:44:56,151 --> 00:44:58,153
Clara, prepare 20 million pesos.

870
00:44:58,237 --> 00:44:59,822
[Clara] <i>Twenty million, Mayor?</i>

871
00:44:59,905 --> 00:45:01,198
[Arnaldo] Yes, 20 million.

872
00:45:01,281 --> 00:45:04,451
[Clara] <i>But, Mayor, we have to</i>
<i>inform the congressman first.</i>

873
00:45:04,535 --> 00:45:05,869
Listen to me.

874
00:45:05,953 --> 00:45:07,704
You don't need Grandpa's signature, right?

875
00:45:10,457 --> 00:45:11,708
Just do as I say.

876
00:45:12,876 --> 00:45:17,339
[unsettling music playing]

877
00:45:21,593 --> 00:45:22,636
Ivy?

878
00:45:29,560 --> 00:45:34,064
[suspenseful music playing]

879
00:45:40,529 --> 00:45:41,530
Ivy!

880
00:45:42,197 --> 00:45:43,449
[mumbles] Where are you?

881
00:45:43,532 --> 00:45:44,533
Where…

882
00:45:45,242 --> 00:45:50,664
[suspenseful music playing]

883
00:46:06,096 --> 00:46:12,769
[suspenseful music playing]

884
00:46:24,072 --> 00:46:25,073
Hands up.

885
00:46:25,741 --> 00:46:27,201
Uh… [laughs]

886
00:46:27,576 --> 00:46:28,952
[Arnaldo grunts]

887
00:46:29,786 --> 00:46:31,038
All right, all right.

888
00:46:31,705 --> 00:46:33,248
[Arnaldo] But you'll regret this.

889
00:46:34,124 --> 00:46:37,002
I don't know where you're
getting the guts to do this.

890
00:46:37,961 --> 00:46:39,588
But you will regret this.

891
00:46:39,671 --> 00:46:41,173
Do you hear me?

892
00:46:41,673 --> 00:46:43,509
Do you hear me?! You will regret this!

893
00:46:43,592 --> 00:46:44,843
[screams and grunts]

894
00:46:46,553 --> 00:46:51,808
[suspenseful music playing]

895
00:46:55,854 --> 00:46:58,398
[car engine revving]

896
00:46:59,399 --> 00:47:01,568
[Jepoy] <i>What did you two talk about?</i>

897
00:47:01,652 --> 00:47:03,695
<i>Will you sell Jaguar out?</i>

898
00:47:03,779 --> 00:47:05,739
[Arthur] <i>Think twice about</i>
<i>everything you're going to do.</i>

899
00:47:05,822 --> 00:47:10,327
<i>You don't want to marry</i>
<i>a corpse, now do you?</i>

900
00:47:11,495 --> 00:47:12,371
[grunts]

901
00:47:12,454 --> 00:47:15,541
<i>Do you know what I do</i>
<i>to traitors like you?</i>

902
00:47:15,624 --> 00:47:17,125
<i>I cut them in half.</i>

903
00:47:17,209 --> 00:47:18,794
[grunts and groans]

904
00:47:18,877 --> 00:47:20,504
[Julio] <i>I want you to do me a favor.</i>

905
00:47:20,587 --> 00:47:25,759
<i>I want you to mount a manhunt</i>
<i>against this hoodlum Jaguar.</i>

906
00:47:25,842 --> 00:47:29,429
<i>I want you to find him,</i>
<i>catch him, and kill him</i>

907
00:47:29,513 --> 00:47:31,390
<i>ASAP.</i>

908
00:47:31,890 --> 00:47:35,102
[theme music playing]
